  "slug": "immunoglobulin-topic-4ec4",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a published B-cell epitope predictor pair 3D structure inputs with learned residue representations for immune recognition.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is learned models that map sequence or 3D structure onto immune recognition outcomes. EpiRanha couples ESM-2 residue embeddings with an E(n)-equivariant graph neural network over 3D structures to score and rank epitope similarity, and is reported to outperform TM-align. MsgaBpred predicts B-cell epitopes from sequence alone by combining AlphaFold3-predicted structures, multi-scale graph convolutions, attention, and ESM-C embeddings. ContinualTCR addresses shifting epitope data in TCR-peptide binding prediction by combining reservoir replay with EWC regularization, reducing forgetting 62.9% relative to fine-tuning. What is new is the pairing of structure-aware representation learning with continual training strategies for evolving epitope data.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-04-29"
}
